# The build context is the patched swipl-devel tree, and this file makes it the
# tree upstream's recipe builds from: npm-swipl-wasm clones swipl-devel without
# --recursive and initialises exactly twelve package submodules
# (docker/Dockerfile at the commit tools/wasm-host/wasm.pin names:
#   packages/chr packages/clib packages/clpqr packages/http packages/json
#   packages/nlp packages/pcre packages/plunit packages/sgml packages/RDF
#   packages/semweb packages/zlib).
# tools/pymetta-host/fetch-source.sh checks out every submodule, because the
# native host builds far more. Handing that tree over as it stands gives cmake
# packages/utf8proc, which is in SWI's WASM package list, and its CMakeLists
# stops on `find_package(PkgConfig REQUIRED)` in an image with no pkg-config
# [measured 2026-09-23: the first build of this image failed there]. No
# swipl-wasm release has ever carried it, so the answer is the upstream
# package set, not a new dependency.
#
# The excluded entries are submodules upstream leaves empty; the plain files
# under packages/ (README, cmake/, index.html) are kept, as a clone has them.
bench
debian
packages/*
!packages/README
!packages/cmake
!packages/index.html
!packages/chr
!packages/clib
!packages/clpqr
!packages/http
!packages/json
!packages/nlp
!packages/pcre
!packages/plunit
!packages/sgml
!packages/RDF
!packages/semweb
!packages/zlib
